CHARACTERS:
Young Dik-dik: A small, tan-colored antelope with large ears and short, thin horns.
Thomson's Gazelle: A brown antelope with large ears and two thin black horns, white underbelly, and black side stripes.
Male Lion: A majestic lion with a shaggy mane and golden fur.
Mongooses: A small, furry, yellow-brown mongoose with a reddish-pink nose and large, round eyes, standing upright on a log.
Ostriches: Large birds with long necks and legs, black and white feathers.
Impala: A young antelope with large ears and short, spiky horns, light brown fur.
Cheetahs: Yellow fur with black spots, some with fluffy manes.
Vultures: Large birds with dark brown feathers, pink heads, and sharp beaks.
Wildebeest: Large antelopes with distinctive dark gray coats and curved horns.
Zebras: Animals with distinctive black and white stripes.
Giraffes: Tall animals with long necks and distinctive brown and white spots.
Jackals: Brown and black canines with pointed ears and bushy tails.
Bat-eared Fox: Small, tan-colored foxes with large, black-tipped ears and bushy tails.
Hartebeest: Brown antelopes with black markings on their legs and faces, and curved horns.
Meerkat: Small, light-brown mongooses with darker stripes on their backs and white faces with dark eyes and black noses.
Hornbill: A bird with a distinctive yellow beak and red facial skin, white and black feathers.
Ibis: A black bird with a long, curved beak and long legs.
Lapwing: A black and white bird with a red beak and yellow legs.
